CDEPS: ESMF trace regions for data-model stream initialisation (diagnostic only)

Purely additive. No existing line is modified or removed; the only new code is
ESMF_TraceRegionEnter/Exit calls and comments, so this cannot change model
results. The new regions nest under the existing datm_strdata_init /
drof_strdata_init entries in ESMF_Profile.summary -- no new output files, no
new tooling, no namelist.

Why: on ACCESS-OM3 at 8 km, datm_strdata_init is 114.8 s of a 866.7 s 1-day run
(13% of wall, 50% of all initialisation) and is one opaque block. It brackets
dshr_mesh_init plus all of shr_strdata_init_from_config, and loop_over_streams1
has no timers or log writes whatsoever.

What you get in ESMF_Profile.summary:

  datm_strdata_init                        1
    strdata_modelmesh                      1   model mesh read (dshr_mesh_init)
    strdata_modelmask                      1   only if maskfile /= meshfile
    strdata_readxml                        1   stream xml / esmfconfig parse
    strdata_modeldomain                    1   shr_strdata_init_model_domain
    strdata_streamloop                     1   shr_strdata_init, whole loop
      strdata_streammesh             n_streams per-stream ESMF_MeshCreate
      strdata_fldbun                 n_streams per-stream field bundle creation
      strdata_regridstore            n_streams per-stream ESMF_FieldRegridStore

The two per-stream Counts are the question being asked. ESMF_MeshCreate
(dshr_strdata_mod.F90:505) and ESMF_FieldRegridStore (640-693) both run once per
stream with no cache. ACCESS-OM3 8 km has 9 DATM streams that all name the same
JRA55do-datm-ESMFmesh.nc, all regrid to the same 4320x3672 model mesh, and use
two distinct mapalgo values (consf x4, patch x5) -- so 9 identical mesh reads
where 1 would do, and 9 weight generations where 2 would do. DROF repeats it
smaller: 2 streams, both consd, one mesh.

Caveat: strdata_fldbun and strdata_regridstore span blocks containing
if (ChkErr(...)) return, so on an error path they exit without closing and that
run's profile is unbalanced. The other six regions are enter/call/exit with no
return in between. An error aborts the run anyway.

Touches dshr/dshr_mod.F90 and streams/dshr_strdata_mod.F90.

